From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:16:29 +0200
Subject: nv30: on the PS3, an indexed draw past the kernel's per-binding cap
 is drawn in pieces

ps3rsx copies the indices each index buffer binding draws into its own ring and refuses a binding
whose primitives span more than 1 MiB of indices (its IXS_MAX; no GETPARAM gives it). A draw of
524032 U32 indices (midprim's elements case, 2 MiB) was refused at every submission: Mesa re-sent
its state and the draws were lost, with no GL error.

On the PS3 (NV30_PS3_IDX_SPLIT, on by default; 0 as before) nv30_draw_elements now draws such a
draw as pieces, each with its own IDXBUF_OFFSET/FORMAT at the 256-byte step at or below its first
index and at most 1 MiB - 4 KiB of indices, so with the kernel's skew (its copy starts up to 255
bytes early) every binding stays under the cap (nv30_idx_split.h):

- Lists are cut on primitive boundaries, line strips with one index of overlap, triangle and quad
  strips with two, each piece starting an even number of indices into its strip so the winding
  holds.
- With primitive restart the cut goes right after the last restart index in the window when it
  has one; otherwise it is counted from the last restart, where a list's grouping and a strip's
  alternation start again. The pieces keep their restart indices and the GPU restarts on them.
- Fans, polygons and line loops share their first vertex across any cut: they are written as a
  triangle (line) list into the upload buffer (restart indices consumed, each triangle's provoking
  vertex the one GL gives it, last or first convention) and that list is split.

The kernel also refuses a submission whose index copies pass the file's share of its ring (1.25
MiB), so two pieces never share one: a piece that would pass it, counting the copies of the
indexed draws since the last kick as the kernel lays them out, is kicked into a submission of its
own (the kernel reuses a copy for the same range, so the count can only overestimate).

NV30_PS3_IDX_STATS counts split draws, conversions, kicks between pieces and draws that could not
be split. The
winsys's line for a cancelled submission now says that its draws are lost and that dmesg says why.

Forwarded: no

